WEBVTT

00:01:36.650 --> 00:01:38.620
<i>We're no match for that Supra.</i>

00:01:39.710 --> 00:01:44.320
<i>But we can't just leave it at that, Z.</i>

00:01:50.650 --> 00:01:52.380
<i>I knew it, it's tonight...</i>

00:01:55.050 --> 00:01:58.600
<i>The Z, Supra and BlackBird...</i>

00:01:58.600 --> 00:02:01.390
<i>The ultimate rivalry between the three monster machines.</i>

00:02:10.700 --> 00:02:12.710
Do you know the Supra driver?

00:02:12.710 --> 00:02:16.200
Yeah. He's the son of an old friend.

00:02:16.760 --> 00:02:18.820
At least, I know the name.

00:02:18.820 --> 00:02:24.220
He's the only son of the late "ultimate demon runner", Aizawa Koichi.

00:02:24.220 --> 00:02:26.240
I know that.

00:02:26.240 --> 00:02:28.390
Is it alright for me to drive seriously?

00:02:28.390 --> 00:02:31.770
Of course, go all out.

00:02:31.770 --> 00:02:35.860
My bonds with people don't matter in your race.

00:03:32.360 --> 00:03:34.300
<i>The BlackBird in front...</i>

00:03:34.300 --> 00:03:35.870
<i>and the Z behind me.</i>

00:03:45.160 --> 00:03:49.940
<i>Stall</i>

00:03:55.220 --> 00:03:58.890
<i>Not bad. He's able to tailgate on such a narrow road.</i>

00:03:58.890 --> 00:04:03.880
<i>That car's not bad either.
At top gear, it could easily reach 200 to 250.</i>

00:04:03.880 --> 00:04:05.910
<i>With enough power, the "Power Band" will be wide.</i>

00:04:05.910 --> 00:04:08.390
<i>The torque characteristics are stable and strong too.</i>

00:04:09.900 --> 00:04:12.390
<i>He has the skill to drive it, too.</i>

00:04:12.390 --> 00:04:15.660
<i>But, his opponent's not any normal guy.</i>

00:04:16.190 --> 00:04:17.660
<i>For example...</i>

00:04:18.570 --> 00:04:21.990
<i>if he wanted to destroy the car in front,</i>

00:04:21.990 --> 00:04:24.160
<i>he'd absolutely do it.</i>

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:29.170
<i>Analyzing the situation in front of him, remaining calm.</i>

00:04:29.170 --> 00:04:32.670
<i>He'll carve a path of his own survival,</i>

00:04:32.670 --> 00:04:35.420
<i>regardless of whether it's at 100km/h or 300km/h.</i>

00:04:39.030 --> 00:04:41.770
<i>The battles he's been through can't compete with this.</i>

00:04:44.320 --> 00:04:47.300
<i>It's very different than relying on skills he learned on his own.</i>

00:05:01.140 --> 00:05:03.540
<i>That bend is very important.</i>

00:05:03.540 --> 00:05:06.160
<i>If the body cannot maneuver the bend,</i>

00:05:06.160 --> 00:05:09.800
<i>going straight would be difficult, let alone drifting.</i>

00:05:09.800 --> 00:05:13.100
<i>If it's too fast it won't do, if it's too slow it's even worse.</i>

00:05:13.100 --> 00:05:14.910
<i>Judgment is very important.</i>

00:05:14.910 --> 00:05:16.300
<i>Can this be done?</i>

00:05:16.980 --> 00:05:19.540
<i>This... could be rather difficult.</i>

00:05:20.270 --> 00:05:22.710
<i>This is closely related to the lifespan of the car's body.</i>

00:05:22.710 --> 00:05:25.460
<i>If the car body exceeds limitations
it would become very troublesome.</i>

00:05:25.460 --> 00:05:29.110
<i>Nevermind. It's alright if it's wasted,
as long as you can make is usable.</i>

00:05:30.680 --> 00:05:33.800
<i>If you just worry about the lifespan of the body,</i>

00:05:33.800 --> 00:05:35.860
<i>how are you going to be able to make it look good?</i>

00:05:37.630 --> 00:05:41.820
<i>Takagi, by now you should know what to do, right?</i>

00:05:41.820 --> 00:05:44.660
<i>Back then you also knew what to do,</i>

00:05:44.660 --> 00:05:46.240
<i>but it wasn't your best.</i>

00:05:47.470 --> 00:05:50.860
<i>Because you love cars more than life.</i>

00:05:57.130 --> 00:06:02.170
<i>The boot has been modified, it should be easier to maneuver now.</i>

00:06:02.170 --> 00:06:03.850
<i>In order to withstand the 800hp surge.</i>

00:06:03.850 --> 00:06:07.360
<i>I sacrificed your car's body to reduce the resistance.</i>

00:06:09.400 --> 00:06:14.390
<i>Takagi, you love cars more than life
itself, so was that really ok with you?</i>

00:06:14.390 --> 00:06:21.210
<i>The engine performance is overwhelming,
the job was done too perfectly.</i>

00:06:21.990 --> 00:06:27.160
<i>Yamamoto, Ota, aren't you supposed to be scary people?</i>

00:06:28.520 --> 00:06:31.210
<i>To Kei, does it even matter?</i>

00:06:31.860 --> 00:06:36.320
<i>No matter what happens, you must live on.</i>

00:06:36.320 --> 00:06:40.670
<i>Isn't this what Aizawa wanted to convey the most?</i>

00:06:45.970 --> 00:06:50.760
<i>The Supra's boot is already showing signs of folding.</i>

00:06:54.760 --> 00:06:58.040
<i>When the boot is distorted, it'll temporarily lose power.</i>

00:06:58.040 --> 00:07:02.280
<i>But after that, it won't be distorted anymore.
It'll accept the driving force and move forward.</i>

00:07:02.280 --> 00:07:05.280
<i>The distorted body will push the car forward.</i>

00:07:05.280 --> 00:07:08.030
<i>Under distortion, it will undertake the loss of power.</i>

00:07:10.040 --> 00:07:13.330
<i>I can do it, with this monster Supra.</i>

00:07:13.330 --> 00:07:15.540
<i>I'll defeat BlackBird!</i>

00:07:23.090 --> 00:07:25.580
Do you know, Kitami-san...

00:07:25.580 --> 00:07:30.850
That Supra's currently known as the strongest on the C1 loop line.

00:07:30.850 --> 00:07:34.340
Do you want to make a break past your opponent?

00:07:41.860 --> 00:07:45.760
<i>The steering wheel and tires are
communicating with me, this feeling...</i>

00:07:45.760 --> 00:07:48.870
<i>it feels like no matter what happens, I'll catch up.</i>

00:07:50.870 --> 00:07:52.380
<i>Now!</i>

00:07:52.700 --> 00:07:55.880
This is fantastic, Takagi-sama.

00:07:56.440 --> 00:07:58.710
The Supra is amazing.

00:07:58.710 --> 00:08:00.870
Such a strong edge makes the opponent even more challenging.

00:08:01.330 --> 00:08:03.890
It highlights another type of perfection.

00:08:03.890 --> 00:08:06.880
Then, you also understand the price of perfection, right?

00:08:08.100 --> 00:08:11.390
That car will die very quickly.

00:08:11.390 --> 00:08:15.390
When the peak is reached, that car will die.

00:08:15.390 --> 00:08:20.400
The man they call the god of car body mods made it.

00:08:24.910 --> 00:08:26.330
<i>Left?</i>

00:08:26.330 --> 00:08:27.940
<i>U-turn at the C1 loop?</i>

00:08:46.460 --> 00:08:51.930
<i>All the other racers have gone their own way.</i>

00:08:55.740 --> 00:08:57.710
<i>I'm the only one left.</i>

00:08:57.710 --> 00:09:01.200
<i>Yet, I'm experiencing the thrill of my life...</i>

00:09:02.110 --> 00:09:04.900
<i>racing against the strongest opponent!</i>

00:09:13.450 --> 00:09:19.450
<i>Splendid, did didn't overtake me easily at this critical point, but...</i>

00:09:21.220 --> 00:09:22.950
<i>It's over...</i>

00:09:22.950 --> 00:09:26.770
<i>Have you noticed? That car's already dead.</i>

00:09:26.770 --> 00:09:28.520
<i>It's a little different now.</i>

00:09:28.520 --> 00:09:34.760
<i>Engine's still powerful, it can still smoothly
move forward but it's just different.</i>

00:09:44.270 --> 00:09:45.480
Huh?

00:09:51.490 --> 00:09:53.280
<i>Damn it! I still can make it!</i>

00:09:56.030 --> 00:10:00.830
<i>The Supra's actions have changed, it's becoming dangerous now.</i>

00:10:00.930 --> 00:10:01.830
<i>What now... </i>

00:10:03.500 --> 00:10:04.830
<i>it's too messy.</i>

00:10:27.350 --> 00:10:29.710
<i>Why, even after that...</i>

00:10:29.710 --> 00:10:31.370
Because of Z.

00:10:31.370 --> 00:10:35.020
The shadow of Z is driving him on.

00:10:37.620 --> 00:10:40.860
Sparing nothing while stepping into the
danger of the world beyond his limits.

00:10:46.280 --> 00:10:49.380
<i>Kei, that car's already dead.</i>

00:10:49.380 --> 00:10:52.120
<i>You should be able to hear the cries of it's body.</i>

00:10:52.680 --> 00:10:57.300
<i>That car's already dead, it can't even move straight.</i>

00:11:13.120 --> 00:11:16.800
<i>Kei, who do you want to become?</i>

00:11:18.430 --> 00:11:22.150
<i>Kei, stop chasing my shadow.</i>

00:11:22.790 --> 00:11:26.380
<i>That's enough. You should walk your own path.</i>

00:11:26.380 --> 00:11:31.300
<i>You are who you are.
You shouldn't try to become somebody else, Kei.</i>

00:11:46.910 --> 00:11:51.500
<i>Kei, have you ever thought about your future?</i>

00:11:52.790 --> 00:11:56.980
<i>Hey, Kei... can I be Kohta's girlfriend?</i>

00:11:57.740 --> 00:12:02.720
<i>You should stop eventually, you're the only one left.</i>

00:12:02.720 --> 00:12:08.310
<i>Something happening to a friend and something
happening to the most important person to you,</i>

00:12:09.410 --> 00:12:11.090
<i>they're very different.</i>

00:12:15.300 --> 00:12:20.800
<i>How much have I lost for this car?</i>

00:12:24.800 --> 00:12:26.560
<i>It's out of control!</i>

00:12:29.170 --> 00:12:31.340
<i>I have to meet Mom.</i>

00:12:33.120 --> 00:12:35.570
<i>I must not let Mom be lonely.</i>

00:12:38.050 --> 00:12:42.570
<i>I understand, I must not die.</i>

00:12:54.130 --> 00:12:56.880
What's wrong? Aren't you overtaking?

00:12:56.880 --> 00:12:58.630
Why did he suddenly...

00:12:59.180 --> 00:13:02.630
Why did he drive that dead car to this point?

00:13:04.630 --> 00:13:07.640
I know what you mean.

00:13:08.440 --> 00:13:12.310
In just one night, stalling for just a moment,

00:13:12.310 --> 00:13:16.340
what lost was not only speed.

00:13:17.650 --> 00:13:20.880
You too, Akio too.

00:13:20.880 --> 00:13:26.220
It's very clear that the driver's heart as stalled.

00:13:27.230 --> 00:13:29.270
He can no longer race.

00:13:37.620 --> 00:13:41.930
Take a look here, it's already badly folding in.

00:13:41.930 --> 00:13:46.140
The car body is totally distorted, it can no longer race.

00:13:46.140 --> 00:13:52.650
But it's because of races that demand such
a car body, that it exists in the first place.

00:13:55.910 --> 00:13:58.390
In layman's terms,

00:13:58.390 --> 00:14:01.410
probably that's why everybody did this.

00:14:02.660 --> 00:14:03.910
Probably...

00:14:10.910 --> 00:14:14.950
As a last resort to save Kei...

00:14:14.950 --> 00:14:20.430
and to let him give up, you made such a car.

00:14:20.430 --> 00:14:24.570
The driver and the car had no accident.
They made the same decision.

00:14:24.570 --> 00:14:27.670
The result of ultra professional modification.

00:14:27.670 --> 00:14:31.180
If Aizawa was still alive, he would have wanted this as well.

00:14:34.400 --> 00:14:37.910
Perhaps you all turned into weird old men.

00:14:37.910 --> 00:14:41.860
Using your combined modification skills,

00:14:41.860 --> 00:14:47.770
you created a monster machine that would
die, but still run at 300km/h for Kei.

00:14:48.850 --> 00:14:50.380
But in the end,

00:14:50.380 --> 00:14:56.670
he's lost his heart in just one race.

00:14:57.720 --> 00:15:02.920
Unfortunately, Aizawa Keiichiro has resigned.

00:15:04.230 --> 00:15:07.420
Without teaching him what was most important,

00:15:08.120 --> 00:15:11.970
Kei was dumped into Aizawa's shoes.

00:15:14.470 --> 00:15:20.260
It would be meaningless for him to
jump into a world he could not control.

00:15:20.260 --> 00:15:22.990
That is what Kei himself understood.

00:15:23.750 --> 00:15:26.990
What should have been taught by use modification masters,

00:15:27.890 --> 00:15:30.990
yet we didn't teach him these.

00:15:33.980 --> 00:15:41.000
You didn't teach him to continue racing,
so that he may see clearly.

00:15:42.250 --> 00:15:45.970
The car by your side probably wouldn't
even appear in your dreams.

00:15:46.600 --> 00:15:49.230
That car runs above 300km/h.

00:15:51.060 --> 00:15:52.760
I have no regrets.

00:15:52.760 --> 00:15:56.610
At that point, I already entrusted everything to Z.

00:15:56.610 --> 00:15:58.100
The feeling of being able to continue accelerating,

00:15:59.810 --> 00:16:03.040
protrudes not a single centimeter of distance.

00:16:03.040 --> 00:16:09.830
And the flash in which I caught off with
BlackBird and overtook him...

00:16:10.660 --> 00:16:12.840
I'll never forget it.

00:16:15.300 --> 00:16:16.660
Can I ask you a question?

00:16:17.950 --> 00:16:20.370
How long do you intend to drive this Z?

00:16:20.370 --> 00:16:22.670
Forever.

00:16:23.340 --> 00:16:25.170
Until the very end.

00:16:36.890 --> 00:16:39.610
Why are you taking this bus?

00:16:39.610 --> 00:16:41.340
To attend class, of course.

00:16:41.340 --> 00:16:43.390
Why? Haven't you given up?

00:16:43.390 --> 00:16:45.130
I haven't.

00:16:49.850 --> 00:16:50.860
Here you go.

00:17:00.870 --> 00:17:01.740
This is...

00:17:01.740 --> 00:17:03.820
Your Supra.

00:17:03.820 --> 00:17:05.270
It's no longer mine.

00:17:05.270 --> 00:17:10.500
Go drive. We'd like you to continue racing.

00:17:11.130 --> 00:17:12.430
But, so soon...

00:17:12.430 --> 00:17:15.060
We definitely couldn't retain 800hp,

00:17:15.060 --> 00:17:17.810
but we tuned it down to 400hp which should be sustainable.

00:17:17.810 --> 00:17:20.770
Frankly, the car body couldn't make it.

00:17:20.770 --> 00:17:24.710
But with 400hp, the car can continue racing.

00:17:24.710 --> 00:17:27.270
You probably feel like 400hp is pretty useless.

00:17:27.270 --> 00:17:33.080
The car probably won't make it in the Wangan 300km/h races.

00:17:33.080 --> 00:17:36.790
C1 would rely on your skills, that shouldn't be a problem for you.

00:17:36.790 --> 00:17:38.180
This color...

00:17:38.180 --> 00:17:42.040
Ah, we repainted it with the color you originally didn't want.

00:17:42.510 --> 00:17:44.550
The same color as your dad's, silver.

00:17:55.060 --> 00:17:57.620
I'll race. Forever.

00:17:59.680 --> 00:18:05.340
Because without me... this car wouldn't even go straight.

00:18:16.290 --> 00:18:19.200
Do all the rich and powerful guests drive Porsches?

00:18:19.200 --> 00:18:22.290
After a little modification, it's only slightly fast.
They get worn down quickly, too.

00:18:22.290 --> 00:18:26.070
Anyway, I can no longer catch up with R's speed.

00:18:26.070 --> 00:18:29.250
To begin with, Porsches were never made to run fast.

00:18:29.250 --> 00:18:31.800
They exist.

00:18:31.800 --> 00:18:34.730
BlackBird's one.

00:18:34.730 --> 00:18:36.800
That guy, Kitami Jun, modified his.

00:18:36.800 --> 00:18:39.620
Don't tell me he actually made it faster.

00:18:39.620 --> 00:18:43.540
Kitami... it's been some time since we last heard of him.

00:18:43.540 --> 00:18:46.320
He's probably last generation's modification master.

00:18:46.840 --> 00:18:50.680
Did you know, a woman is behind the wheels of the white R32?

00:18:50.680 --> 00:18:53.830
She recently gained some fame in the city.

00:18:53.830 --> 00:18:55.110
A woman?

00:18:57.220 --> 00:18:58.820
Where are you going?

00:18:58.820 --> 00:19:00.840
I'm going for a spin.

00:19:00.840 --> 00:19:03.830
The traffic's still heavy in the city at this hour.

00:19:03.830 --> 00:19:04.960
Doesn't matter.

00:19:06.840 --> 00:19:09.840
He really loves to race.

00:19:09.840 --> 00:19:13.850
He may love it, but he's still an amateur.

00:19:13.850 --> 00:19:16.220
He doesn't even listen to other's advice.

00:19:16.220 --> 00:19:18.840
It doesn't matter if he's good or bad, Taka's really serious.

00:19:18.840 --> 00:19:22.390
Did you know he's working by himself now?

00:19:22.390 --> 00:19:23.330
By himself?

00:19:23.330 --> 00:19:25.850
Is his shop really not doing that well?

00:19:25.850 --> 00:19:27.830
No, business didn't drop,

00:19:27.830 --> 00:19:30.860
it's actually himself who declined the job.

00:19:30.860 --> 00:19:36.020
He couldn't take the younger worker's irresponsible attitude,

00:19:36.020 --> 00:19:39.610
in everything from changing the oil to welding every screw.

00:19:42.630 --> 00:19:45.630
He couldn't let it go,

00:19:45.630 --> 00:19:47.940
so that's why he's an amateur.

00:19:47.940 --> 00:19:50.570
A professional must have determination and efficiency,

00:19:50.570 --> 00:19:53.130
and some compromise is required as well.

00:19:54.630 --> 00:19:56.130
<i>Horrible.</i>

00:19:56.130 --> 00:19:59.340
<i>The "once a month" meeting that I have to turn up for reluctantly,</i>

00:19:59.340 --> 00:20:02.110
<i>all they do now is talk about the past and grumble to themselves.</i>

00:20:08.980 --> 00:20:10.950
<i>Hmm? An R32 without a tail fin?</i>

00:20:10.950 --> 00:20:14.700
<i>It's my first time seeing one.</i>

00:20:16.710 --> 00:20:18.080
<i>R33?</i>

00:20:20.690 --> 00:20:23.000
<i>Oh... this is good.</i>

00:20:23.000 --> 00:20:26.460
<i>It would be hard to get an opening near the Ginza at the front.</i>

00:20:27.630 --> 00:20:29.460
<i>Not that I want to get involved,</i>

00:20:29.460 --> 00:20:35.800
<i>but at this place and time with that R around, I think I will.</i>

00:20:42.300 --> 00:20:45.300
<i>Side by side... good, let me see...</i>

00:20:47.320 --> 00:20:50.310
<i>A woman? It must be the one in the stories...</i>

00:20:55.330 --> 00:20:58.820
<i>I've lost her! Don't look down on me!</i>

00:20:58.820 --> 00:21:01.540
<i>The car's powerful and her skills are good.</i>

00:21:01.540 --> 00:21:03.580
<i>Just who on Earth is this woman?</i>

00:21:06.590 --> 00:21:09.840
<i>That moment of carelessness completely changed things around.</i>

00:21:09.840 --> 00:21:13.670
<i>The control of the brake, the closeness of the corner,</i>

00:21:13.670 --> 00:21:17.040
<i>everything is so perfect, there's no way I can pass.</i>

00:21:18.840 --> 00:21:22.880
Starting from Hamasaki Bridge, the interchange bridge
connecting to Wangan. Once I've entered Wangan...

00:21:30.530 --> 00:21:33.140
I've found them. The guys who modified the white R32.

00:21:33.140 --> 00:21:34.820
Where's it from, then?

00:21:34.820 --> 00:21:39.920
Yamamoto Cars. Recently, they put back
up their signs saying "Yamamoto Speed".

00:21:39.920 --> 00:21:44.540
Speaking of which, RGO recently restarted their old business too.

00:21:44.540 --> 00:21:47.340
Yatabe's gained back their reputation as well.

00:21:49.700 --> 00:21:52.420
Hey, is it alright for us to stay like this?

00:21:53.860 --> 00:21:56.100
Weren't we much more enthusiastic in the past?

00:21:56.100 --> 00:21:58.320
Be it Yatabe, Tsukuba or the streets,

00:21:58.320 --> 00:22:00.470
we used to strive to produce the highest speed figures.

00:22:00.470 --> 00:22:02.040
So what?

00:22:02.040 --> 00:22:06.980
BlackBird has Kitami. R32 has Yamamoto, Yatabe has Ohta.

00:22:06.980 --> 00:22:10.480
They are all old-timers.

00:22:11.080 --> 00:22:12.970
That's true.

00:22:12.970 --> 00:22:14.350
Let's do this!

00:22:14.350 --> 00:22:15.120
Interesting!

00:22:15.120 --> 00:22:18.990
Alright, let's try aiming for that R32 first.

00:22:19.530 --> 00:22:21.460
Let's show them our power.

00:22:21.460 --> 00:22:26.700
Let's drive the outdated Kitami and Yamamoto out of the industry!

00:22:29.870 --> 00:22:32.000
<i>She totally disappeared.</i>

00:22:32.800 --> 00:22:35.050
<i>Well, I'll enter Daikoku first.</i>

00:22:42.810 --> 00:22:47.300
<i>What's with the car coming up from behind? Overtaking like this?</i>

00:22:47.300 --> 00:22:50.630
<i>No. It's not overtaking. Then what?</i>

00:22:50.630 --> 00:22:52.300
<i>It's catching up to me?</i>

00:22:52.920 --> 00:22:56.320
<i>Wait a minute. I've just cut my speed.</i>

00:22:56.800 --> 00:23:00.650
<i>I entered the Wangan at around 250km/h.</i>

00:23:01.370 --> 00:23:04.620
<i>Just exactly how fast is this car driving?</i>
